 "notes": "Cai at the mouth of Lac Bay: the beach entry by the conch-shell piles, the steep slope into the Lac entrance channel within 20-30 m of the shore, the sand channel to 25-30 m where tarpon gather, giant anemones and hard coral between 8 and 20 m, and the barrier reef on the far side (bonaire.com Cai page). The channel outline is approximate; the anemone and tarpon spots are placed by assumption, and no route is drawn because the current decides it: start against it and let it carry you back. Coastline and reef outline © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL). Positions are approximate.",
